# Auto-update GitHub (BitWieser)

When the user finishes a change in this repo, or asks to save/sync/push, update GitHub without being asked again.

1. `git status` and `git diff`. Do not commit `.env`, `uploads/`, `desktop/release/`, `desktop/pack/`, `node_modules`, `dist`, or `*.exe`.
2. Stage the relevant source files.
3. Commit with a short message that says why the change exists.
4. `git push -u origin HEAD` to https://github.com/Priyanshucodes-100/BitWieser.git
5. Tell the user the commit hash and that `main` is updated.

Do not force-push. Do not amend a commit that is already on GitHub. If push fails on auth, say so and stop.
